# Button group order

When two or more buttons sit together in a group, order by priority. “Primary / secondary / tertiary” means **action emphasis**, not `Button` `variant="secondary"` (that variant is banned — use `outline`).

- **Default (left / start aligned):** primary → secondary → tertiary (left to right)
- **Right-aligned groups** (`justify-end`, `DialogFooter`, `AlertDialogFooter`, `ml-auto`, etc.): reverse that order so primary sits on the right edge (secondary → primary)

Destructive actions follow the same priority ladder (usually after the primary affirmative, before weaker tertiary actions—or last when they are the least emphasized).

Segmented controls / mutually exclusive toggles (e.g. Assistant | Physician, Today | Full week) are not action-priority groups; keep a stable logical order.

See `design.md` → UI copy → Button groups.
